Project 4

Resources and documentation:
    I used my previous projects, the course material, and some documentation from cplusplus.com:
        Vector documentation:
            https://cplusplus.com/reference/vector/vector/erase/#google_vignette
        
AI Usage:
    I only used Chat GPT for quick documentation on vector and stack methods.
        
How to compile:
    1. make sure you are in the "Gavin-Dennis-P4/" directory
    2. in the terminal, run the "make" command to compile the programs
    3. Optionally, run the following commands to execute the program with the following
       test cases: (documentation about test cases at the bottom of this page)
        * make none - runs P4 with tests/P4_test1 (a file that doesn't exist) as an argument
        * make test - runs P4 with cin instead of a file
        * make test1 - runs P4 with tests/P4_test1 as argument
        * make test2 - runs P4 with tests/P4_test2 as argument
        * make test3 - runs P4 with tests/P4_test3 as argument
        * make test4 - runs P4 with tests/P4_test4 as argument
        * make testGavin - runs P4 with tests/P4_testGavin as argument (the most comprehensive test)
    4. the finished executuble 'P4' can be found in the 'build' directory (Gavin-Dennis-P4/build/)

Problems encountered:
    Nested operations and the loop construct were very tricky. I implemented what I would consider a workaround as I'm not sure this was the proper way.
    However, my program passed all four test cases from P2 including the one with the for loop (Test 4). My personal test files showed that my program could
    handle multiple loops, including ones that get skipped due to having a non-positive value or having a non-positive amount of loop iterations.

    After several hours of deep thought, I was able to get nested addition to
    work using a stack structure. Again, not sure if this was the intended fix, but
    it seemed to get the job done for several hard test cases.

    I'm not super proud of this work compared to my previous projects, but I did the best I could with my busy schedule.
    I'm happy that I didn't need to use any AI generated code and felt like I learned alot throughout the creation
    of this project.

Test cases:
    P4_test1.txt - based on test example 1 from P2.
    P4_test2.txt - based on test example 2 from P2.
    P4_test3.txt - based on test example 3 from P2.
    P4_test4.txt - based on test example 4 from P2.
	P4_testGavin - My personal test file. I tried to make it as
                   complicated as I reasonably could with my limited
                   time